From: OpenStack Incus maintainers <openstack-incus@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] hardware: Accept an Incus Manila share transport

Nova's server-share API currently treats virtiofs as the only possible
transport. System containers expose the same Manila attachment through a
restricted Incus disk bind mount and must not advertise the virtiofs trait.
Accept the driver-specific trait without weakening the existing libvirt
checks.

diff --git a/nova/virt/hardware.py b/nova/virt/hardware.py
--- a/nova/virt/hardware.py
+++ b/nova/virt/hardware.py
@@ -3063,6 +3063,7 @@ def check_shares_supported(context, instance):
     trait_info = client.get_provider_traits(context, host.uuid)
 
     if not (
+        'CUSTOM_INCUS_MANILA_SHARE' in trait_info.traits or
         (
             'COMPUTE_STORAGE_VIRTIO_FS' in trait_info.traits and
             'COMPUTE_MEM_BACKING_FILE' in trait_info.traits
